cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use any Trinity VSA discoveries, please cite our defensive publication."
title: "VSA Operations for Ternary Computing"
abstract: "Vector Symbolic Architecture requires high-dimensional representations that are computationally expensive on binary hardware. Existing VSA implementations don't exploit ternary computing's natural alignment with {-1,0,+1} representations for efficiency gains. We present ternary VSA operations using HybridBigInt SIMD achieving 11.87× speedup (p<0.001) versus scalar baselines with cosine similarity in [-1,+1] range. Our implementation includes bind/unbind for associative memory, bundle operations (2-ary/3-ary) for majority voting with noise resilience, ternary dot-product for optimized {-1,0,+1} arithmetic, cyclic permutation for position-independent encoding, and text encoding mapping characters to Vec32i8 hypervectors. Test coverage: 11/11 tests passing (100%) including bind/unbind/bundle/cosine/similarity verification. This enables efficient hyperdimensional computing on ternary hardware with 512D hypervectors and sub-microsecond operation latency."
